content:
E10 confirms:

- ORD-00143: invoice created at t=80, synced at t=90 — entirely before the deploy (t=436) and before Raqib's watch (t=300). This is a pre-existing bad row, not caused by the deploy.
- ORD-00854 and ORD-00859: invoices created at t=437 and t=440 (both after the v1.1 deploy at t=436), synced at t=450. These are caused by the deploy.

ORD-00143's bad data (vat=164.62 vs expected 1097.5×0.15=164.625 — actually that rounds correctly... wait: 1097.5×0.15=164.625, rounded to 2dp=164.63 ≠ 164.62) was written at t=80/90, long before any deploy, indicating bad_input from the supplier document. ORD-00854 (vat=634.56 vs 95.18×0.15=14.28) is wildly wrong — clearly a prompt/extraction error post-deploy.

These are two independent root causes.

